WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.357 --> 00:00:02.940
(upbeat music)

00:00:06.981 --> 00:00:08.952
- Hi, I'm Hannah, your
friendly neighborhood wine mom

00:00:08.952 --> 00:00:10.365
welcome to my couch.

00:00:10.365 --> 00:00:12.275
Pour yourself a glass
of wine and let's talk.

00:00:12.275 --> 00:00:14.144
We did a video awhile
back where you guys could

00:00:14.144 --> 00:00:17.485
text me, and a lot of you
were texting ideas for

00:00:17.485 --> 00:00:18.785
future videos.

00:00:18.785 --> 00:00:20.053
So a text that kept coming through

00:00:20.053 --> 00:00:21.183
is actually tonight's topic.

00:00:21.183 --> 00:00:23.608
Things That I Wish Someone
Had Told Me Before I Had Kids.

00:00:23.608 --> 00:00:25.145
Mmmmmmmm.

00:00:25.145 --> 00:00:27.603
So for me, the number one
thing that I wish someone had

00:00:27.603 --> 00:00:30.212
told me about becoming a mother was how

00:00:30.212 --> 00:00:32.053
it would impact me psychologically.

00:00:32.053 --> 00:00:33.707
Like when you think about
having kids, you think,

00:00:33.707 --> 00:00:35.089
oh my gosh, I'm gonna be tired.

00:00:35.089 --> 00:00:36.997
It's gonna be a lot of responsibility.

00:00:36.997 --> 00:00:39.239
It's gonna be a financial responsibility.

00:00:39.239 --> 00:00:42.104
But you don't think about
what it's going to do

00:00:42.104 --> 00:00:44.066
to you psychologically.

00:00:44.066 --> 00:00:47.175
I don't know what it is
about becoming a mother

00:00:47.175 --> 00:00:50.019
that made me feel like
everything all of a sudden

00:00:50.019 --> 00:00:51.218
needs to be perfect.

00:00:51.218 --> 00:00:52.742
And all of a sudden I need to be perfect.

00:00:52.742 --> 00:00:55.464
And I hold myself to these crazy standards

00:00:55.464 --> 00:00:57.911
as a mother, because I feel
like I have two children

00:00:57.911 --> 00:01:00.959
who look to me on what
to do, and rely on me

00:01:00.959 --> 00:01:03.275
and everything I do has to be perfect.

00:01:03.275 --> 00:01:05.115
I am a working mom.

00:01:05.115 --> 00:01:06.523
I work full-time.

00:01:06.523 --> 00:01:08.029
It's really tough.

00:01:08.029 --> 00:01:09.910
I wake up at 6:30 in the morning

00:01:09.910 --> 00:01:12.572
I try to get myself ready
while I get the kids ready.

00:01:12.572 --> 00:01:14.481
Try to get them to daycare on time.

00:01:14.481 --> 00:01:15.843
Try to get to work on time.

00:01:15.843 --> 00:01:18.403
Work all day, try not to
check my phone too much

00:01:18.403 --> 00:01:20.159
to like deal with all the other kid stuff.

00:01:20.159 --> 00:01:21.926
Try to get home in time to pick them up.

00:01:21.926 --> 00:01:23.340
Make dinner, put them to bed,

00:01:23.340 --> 00:01:25.148
pass out on the couch, repeat.

00:01:25.148 --> 00:01:27.830
I feel guilty because as a working parent

00:01:27.830 --> 00:01:29.728
I have two huge responsibilities

00:01:29.728 --> 00:01:30.924
I have my children

00:01:30.924 --> 00:01:31.861
and I have my job.

00:01:31.861 --> 00:01:34.096
A lot of the time my job takes away from

00:01:34.096 --> 00:01:36.494
time that I could spend with my children.

00:01:36.494 --> 00:01:39.135
And then on the weekends,
I sometimes I just need

00:01:39.135 --> 00:01:41.268
to spend some time staring at the wall

00:01:41.268 --> 00:01:43.422
and they'll watch cartoons
for a couple hours

00:01:43.422 --> 00:01:45.095
and that even makes me feel like crap.

00:01:45.095 --> 00:01:47.953
And I think social media is
a huge problem when it comes

00:01:47.953 --> 00:01:50.736
to setting unrealistic
expectations for moms.

00:01:50.736 --> 00:01:54.118
Because, we're supposed to
post everything positive

00:01:54.118 --> 00:01:55.479
and everything good.

00:01:55.479 --> 00:01:58.933
And the second someone posts
something bad, or unhappy

00:01:58.933 --> 00:02:00.852
it's like I don't want to see that.

00:02:00.852 --> 00:02:02.996
For example, if you look at my Instagram

00:02:02.996 --> 00:02:05.231
you take this one, for example

00:02:05.231 --> 00:02:08.207
it's me, my boys are both smiling.

00:02:08.207 --> 00:02:11.225
And we're out in nature,
we look super happy.

00:02:11.225 --> 00:02:13.692
What you don't see is my husband

00:02:13.692 --> 00:02:15.897
complaining every five
seconds about having to

00:02:15.897 --> 00:02:17.117
take a picture.

00:02:17.117 --> 00:02:19.576
It's 20 degrees outside,
so we're all freezing

00:02:19.576 --> 00:02:21.465
but we had cute shirts
on so I made my kids

00:02:21.465 --> 00:02:22.725
take their jackets off.

00:02:22.725 --> 00:02:25.691
And, you don't see the 8,000
outtakes of both of them

00:02:25.691 --> 00:02:28.565
frowning and crying and me
about to start crying, as well.

00:02:28.565 --> 00:02:30.771
And of course, we all know
that social media is just

00:02:30.771 --> 00:02:32.843
the highlight reel of people's lives.

00:02:32.843 --> 00:02:35.774
But for me, as a mother,
with so much responsibility

00:02:35.774 --> 00:02:38.958
and these high standards
of perfection, it's really

00:02:38.958 --> 00:02:41.040
detrimental on my self-esteem to be seeing

00:02:41.040 --> 00:02:43.708
all these other moms
just looking so happy,

00:02:43.708 --> 00:02:46.789
so well rested, so
pleased with everything.

00:02:46.789 --> 00:02:48.394
And just, like they
have everything together

00:02:48.394 --> 00:02:50.841
when I feel like half the
time I'm falling apart.

00:02:50.841 --> 00:02:52.995
Seeing all this stuff is just like

00:02:52.995 --> 00:02:55.078
a constant reminder of my

00:02:56.103 --> 00:02:57.294
shortcomings.

00:02:57.294 --> 00:02:59.961
And, it makes me feel like crap.

00:03:07.493 --> 00:03:09.046
But

00:03:09.046 --> 00:03:11.279
the way that I have
started to think about it

00:03:11.279 --> 00:03:14.157
and what I've started to realize is

00:03:14.157 --> 00:03:16.328
it's fine to be just
okay, I always tell people

00:03:16.328 --> 00:03:19.235
I'm the world's okayest mom.

00:03:19.235 --> 00:03:21.024
And I'm so happy with that.

00:03:21.024 --> 00:03:23.747
I mean, you meet my kids,
they're well adjusted kids.

00:03:23.747 --> 00:03:26.182
They are clothed, they
are fed, they are loved,

00:03:26.182 --> 00:03:27.169
they are happy.

00:03:27.169 --> 00:03:29.810
And maybe they ate a box of
mac and cheese last night

00:03:29.810 --> 00:03:31.322
but that's not gonna kill them,

00:03:31.322 --> 00:03:32.512
and at least they ate.

00:03:32.512 --> 00:03:33.345
And, maybe

00:03:34.219 --> 00:03:36.170
they sit on the couch and watch cartoons

00:03:36.170 --> 00:03:37.653
for a few hours, but

00:03:37.653 --> 00:03:40.079
I made sure that they're distracted

00:03:40.079 --> 00:03:43.371
while I freaking like
decompress and lose it

00:03:43.371 --> 00:03:45.655
as a human so that they don't have to

00:03:45.655 --> 00:03:46.886
feel the brunt of that.

00:03:46.886 --> 00:03:50.796
And they don't have to feel
that energy coming from me.

00:03:50.796 --> 00:03:51.629
And,

00:03:53.500 --> 00:03:55.959
maybe I don't volunteer for
everything in their school

00:03:55.959 --> 00:03:59.189
and I'm not there to
pick them up everyday but

00:03:59.189 --> 00:04:00.729
(exhales).

00:04:00.729 --> 00:04:02.190
And maybe I don't
volunteer for their school

00:04:02.190 --> 00:04:03.456
and I'm not there to pick them up everyday

00:04:03.456 --> 00:04:04.927
but that's because I'm working so that

00:04:04.927 --> 00:04:07.069
we have insurance and

00:04:07.069 --> 00:04:08.910
they can see their doctor and

00:04:08.910 --> 00:04:11.488
they can have all their soccer lessons

00:04:11.488 --> 00:04:13.793
and dance classes and all the
stuff that they want to do.

00:04:13.793 --> 00:04:15.225
And college funds and

00:04:15.225 --> 00:04:17.024
I'm doing this all for their future.

00:04:17.024 --> 00:04:19.089
That's not a bad mom, I'm not the world's

00:04:19.089 --> 00:04:20.073
perfect mom

00:04:20.073 --> 00:04:22.641
because I'll never be
the world's perfect mom.

00:04:22.641 --> 00:04:23.659
But I'm okay.

00:04:23.659 --> 00:04:27.386
So I don't know why moms
are so hard on themselves.

00:04:27.386 --> 00:04:31.553
When really even if we're
doing an okay job, that's fine.

00:04:33.169 --> 00:04:35.383
If you are about to have children

00:04:35.383 --> 00:04:37.273
that is my one piece of advice to you.

00:04:37.273 --> 00:04:39.792
And if you already have
children, let yourself off

00:04:39.792 --> 00:04:40.970
the hook a little bit

00:04:40.970 --> 00:04:42.605
and do what you need to do

00:04:42.605 --> 00:04:43.842
to make sure that you are happy.

00:04:43.842 --> 00:04:45.998
Whether it's meditating, or

00:04:45.998 --> 00:04:47.960
planting your kids in front of the TV

00:04:47.960 --> 00:04:50.874
and sitting on the bathroom
floor eating cheesecake.

00:04:50.874 --> 00:04:54.258
Or having a glass of wine,
or whatever you need to do

00:04:54.258 --> 00:04:56.644
to practice self care

00:04:56.644 --> 00:04:58.656
make sure that that's a priority too.

00:04:58.656 --> 00:05:01.532
As long as you are invested,
and you are committed,

00:05:01.532 --> 00:05:04.272
and you are there for your children

00:05:04.272 --> 00:05:06.295
we can fuck up a little bit and it's fine.

00:05:06.295 --> 00:05:08.623
Parents don't have to be perfect.

00:05:08.623 --> 00:05:10.533
Also, I wish someone had told me that

00:05:10.533 --> 00:05:12.939
when newborns crap, it can literally

00:05:12.939 --> 00:05:14.584
leak from their diaper

00:05:14.584 --> 00:05:16.149
all the way up to the back of their head

00:05:16.149 --> 00:05:19.149
because the first time that happened

00:05:20.680 --> 00:05:22.215
it was horrifying.

00:05:22.215 --> 00:05:24.571
(upbeat music)

00:05:24.571 --> 00:05:25.716
So that's all I've got for today.

00:05:25.716 --> 00:05:27.294
I'm Hannah, your friendly
neighborhood wine mom

00:05:27.294 --> 00:05:29.254
and if you have any topic
you want me to talk about

00:05:29.254 --> 00:05:30.444
leave it in the comments.

00:05:30.444 --> 00:05:33.186
And, if you too are the
world's okayest parent

00:05:33.186 --> 00:05:34.670
shout yourself out in the comments

00:05:34.670 --> 00:05:36.243
give yourself a little pat on the back.

00:05:36.243 --> 00:05:38.732
And in the meantime, I'm
gonna finish practicing

00:05:38.732 --> 00:05:40.042
my self care.

00:05:40.042 --> 00:05:41.292
'Til next time.

00:05:42.348 --> 00:05:45.101
Can this be a musical show now?

00:05:45.101 --> 00:05:46.300
Where I'm just like

00:05:46.300 --> 00:05:47.633
this is my wine.

00:05:48.872 --> 00:05:49.705
Mmmmmm.

